### A Few Questions to Guide Us
1. **What contexts matter most to you?** (e.g., professional decisions, personal life, academic study, evaluating media/news, creative problem-solving)
2. **What feels like your biggest current challenge?** (e.g., identifying biases, analyzing arguments deeply, making decisions under uncertainty, communicating your reasoning clearly)
3. **How much time can you realistically dedicate weekly?**
4. **Do you prefer individual reading/reflection, interactive discussions/debate, structured courses, or practical real-world exercises?**

---

### Draft Framework: My Initial Thinking
While you consider those, here's a flexible 3-phase structure I would love to shape with you:

| Phase | Focus | Sample Activities |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Foundation** | Awareness & Metacognition | Journaling assumptions; bias spotting in daily news; simple argument mapping |
| **Practice** | Structured Analysis | Case study breakdowns; Socratic questioning with a study partner; logic puzzles |
| **Application** | Real-World Integration | Pre-mortems on major decisions; debating opposite viewpoints; teaching concepts to others |

---

I would truly love to hear your thoughts on any or all of these questions so I can refine this into your personalized roadmap! What resonates most with you so far?<|im_end|>
